    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23065" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-expĭābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		2. in-expio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that cannot be atoned for</i>, <i>inexpiable</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">religio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 1, 12, 27</span></i>
			: scelus, Auct. Har. Resp. 27.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>implacable</i>,
				<i>irreconcilable</i>, <i>obstinate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bellum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					4, 35, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">41, 24, 7</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 16, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">odium Romanorum in Hannibalem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					39, 51, 4</span></i>
			 Drak. <i>N. cr.;</i> 2, 17, 2: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">invidia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 78</span></i>
			.— <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-expĭābĭlĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>inexpiably</i>, <i>irremediably</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corruptus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. de Gen. ad Litt. 11, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
